---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-hover-card</code> shows a rich preview, such as a profile or a link preview, while the
  pointer rests on its trigger or the trigger has keyboard focus. The first child is the trigger;
  the element with <code>slot="content"</code> is the card. The card can hold links and buttons.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <p>
    Reviewed by
    <wc-hover-card id='hover-card-demo'>
      <a href='#ana-lima'>Ana Lima</a>
      <div slot='content' style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;'>
        <div style='display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;'>
          <wc-avatar name='Ana Lima'></wc-avatar>
          <div>
            <strong>Ana Lima</strong>
            <div>Product designer, Lisbon</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style='margin: 0;'>Works on the design system and the mobile app.</p>
        <div><wc-button size='sm' variant='outlined'>Follow</wc-button></div>
      </div>
    </wc-hover-card>
    yesterday.
  </p>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const card = document.querySelector('#hover-card-demo');
      card.addEventListener('open', () => myConsole.log('open'));
      card.addEventListener('close', event => myConsole.log('close', event.detail.reason));
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Timing</h3>
<p>
  The card opens after <code>open-delay</code> (500 ms), so it does not flash while the pointer
  crosses the page, and closes <code>close-delay</code> (300 ms) after the pointer and focus leave
  both the trigger and the card, so the pointer can move into the card. It stays open while the
  pointer is over it or focus is inside it. Escape and a press outside close it at once.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-hover-card open-delay='150' close-delay='600' placement='top-start'>
    <a href='#release'>Release 3.4</a>
    <div slot='content'>
      <strong>Release 3.4</strong>
      <p style='margin: 0.25rem 0 0;'>12 changes, shipped 6 November.</p>
    </div>
  </wc-hover-card>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>When to use it</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>wc-tooltip</code>: a short plain-text description of a control.</li>
  <li>
    <code>wc-hover-card</code>: a preview of where a link goes, with optional actions. Nothing in it
    may be the only way to do something.
  </li>
  <li><code>wc-popover</code>: content the person opens on purpose, by clicking.</li>
</ul>
